    <string name="qibla_method_note">Directions are true north. Qibla is the shortest path on the Earth\'s ellipsoid (WGS-84) to the Kaaba. Two decimals are shown; the real accuracy is the sensor\'s, shown above.</string>
    <string name="qibla_declination_note">Magnetic declination here: %1$s, applied.</string>
    <string name="cal_title">Calibrate the compass</string>
    <string name="cal_step1">Move away from metal, electronics, speakers and car interiors.</string>
    <string name="cal_step2">Take the phone out of any case or holder with a magnet.</string>
    <string name="cal_step3">Hold the phone and trace a figure eight in the air a few times, turning your wrist.</string>
    <string name="cal_step4">Then rotate the phone slowly a full turn while keeping it flat.</string>
    <string name="cal_step5">Lay it flat and wait a few seconds for the reading to settle.</string>
